  "findings": [
    "With a batch norm layer in the forward path (`units_per_layer` with two or more entries) a seeded fit does not reproduce the 1.6.1 eval-mode predictions to the `train` class (deviation steps of variant `default`); the cause is the zero gradient of the bias in front of the batch norm layer, not a logic difference (see `BATCH_NORM_EXPLANATION`). It is a property of the architecture that v2 inherits unchanged.",
    "The network is the 1.6.1 network, so a `state_dict` of one loads into the other with `strict=True` and the forward pass agrees at the `forward` class in eval and in train mode.",
    "The scaler is the 1.6.1 one: arcsinh, then a `StandardScaler` fit on the distinct training samples (`np.unique(output.cell_line_ids)`); the v2 `scaledGeneExpression` fits on the distinct samples too (`fit_on_unique_ids`).",
    "The v2 preset (commit 174ceea7, B5) sets `gene_list: landmark_genes` on `scaledGeneExpression`, the 1.6.1 default (`SimpleNeuralNetwork.gene_list`). The case does not override it: the v2 side reads the list from the preset, the 1.6.1 side from its class default, and the selected columns agree. Before B5 the preset had no gene list.",
    "The v2 predictor defaults (since B5 (174ceea7)) are the first grid point of 1.6.1: `units_per_layer` [32, 16, 8, 4], `dropout_prob` 0.3, `max_epochs` 100; before them they were [512, 256, 128], 0.2 and 50. The batch size (16) and the patience (5) were hard-coded in 1.6.1 and are v2 hyperparameters. The case sets all of them explicitly on both sides, so it does not depend on the defaults.",
    "1.6.1 loaders use 8 persistent worker processes; the case makes them single-process, which does not change the main-process RNG order. The drop-last rule agrees (`len > batch_size` against `batch_size < n_pairs` after clipping the batch size to the number of pairs)."
  ],
